Z||000000||maryjane||11-22-2001||07:37 AM||||I suppose Cliff could probably answer this best, but I would like some input from others also, if any of you are familar with the topic. I am not. I belong to another board, (military related, mostly retirees) It is HIGHLY moderated. Each thread starter  & reply is reviewed before being actually posted, sometimes takes 48 hrs to actually see it posted. The reason given is "we cannot afford a high dollar lawsuit & the expenses involved in defending ourselves in court. Racial comments, of course are not allowed. (I fully agree with this) What they are screening for (recently), are refrences to foreign cultures or religious views. I'll give you an example that would NOT be accepted, "Kill the sob's and bury them in pig skins, so they can never enter Heaven.".<BR>Now, I understand that this is derogatory, but not sure about being so worried about litigation. Also anything that would cast an 'unprofessional' shadow on the branch of service we are in. (USMC) Are lawsuits generated from, or as a result of, a forum post common or a danger to be considered? I mean, we are all combat veterans on this forum, seems like they want us to act like choirboys, and it is an un-natural thing to do, when you get a couple of hundred Marines together. About 60% of the stuff posted here in OT would be rejected there, & we are getting a litle tired of it. We've lost a lot of long time members. I could change to another forum, but have a lot of friends there. All comments to the webmaster are answered with the same, 'lawsuit' reply. Any comments? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||hugh||11-22-2001||08:36 AM||||When you can be sued for expressing an opinion,whether it is on the internet or in your own home,it will be a sad time for us all.In my mind the internet is just a meeting place and the forums are really nothing more than a means of communication between people who have something in common.Forums are,in a way,like newspapers.They only carry a message.You probably should get together with your friends through Emails(like the underground,so they can't be censored)and find another forum,or start your own.<BR> This forum is the only one I am on,and it means a lot to me.I have made many friends over the last 1 1/2 years(plus a few who don't exactly care for me).It would be hard for me to follow such advice,but if it was the only way,I would give it a try!<BR>Good luck in finding a solution.  ||||reg||14
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||11-22-2001||08:41 AM||||In the United States, you can be sued for *anything*. <P>How successful your case may be (or if it is even deemed worthy to be heard in the first place) is another matter entirely.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||11-22-2001||08:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>In the United States, you can be sued for *anything*. <P>How successful your case may be (or if it is even deemed worthy to be heard in the first place) is another matter entirely.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree Don, it sounds like the moderator of the group is being too sensitive, or his boyfriend is on the rag...<BR>As to cyber lawsuits, a direct attack on a person would be pursueable, but general racial/ethnic type of comments would be in bad taste...<BR>Unless a person can prove you are targeting them with threats/slurs, you probly won't have to worry about a court date...<BR>Besides the "lawsuit reply", does the moderator give a real life situation as to why he is concerned? Has he been involved in such a lawsuit?<BR>Look at the crap that happens here for example, if it gets out of hand, Chris freezes the thread, and I supose he can also remove such threads that could be deemed totally offensive...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||11-22-2001||09:13 AM||||Maybe I put too much emphasis on the example I gave. It's just that we can't post anything that could evolve into a 'lively'<BR>discussion. It's got to the point that it is little more than a place to post up coming events or links to news items. Everyone is afraid to post any personal opinion. The general feeling is that the webmaster/moderators are just too PC. No explanation about the lawsuit thing, just refrences to how much it would cost to defend in court. Bad thing is, it is a members only thing that is costing us $35/yr. There are other benefits to belonging to this organization, bi-yearly reunion, newsletter, etc, but most of us like the 2 forums to communicate. It's very informative, but realistically, not much fun anymore. It's no big thing really, just wondering how likely a lawsuit would be on one of these type things.||||reg||1
